WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.497 --> 00:00:14.902
Zann crashed hard into the ground.

2
00:00:14.922 --> 00:00:16.883
"Ow!" he yelped.

3
00:00:17.603 --> 00:00:21.065
He opened his eyes and rubbed his knee, which had slammed into a rock.

4
00:00:21.786 --> 00:00:24.747
He, his friends, and Wyssa were in a forest clearing.

5
00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.928
"Where are we?"

6
00:00:27.389 --> 00:00:28.009
Perda asked.

7
00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:31.291
"I think we're near Wormwood," Darb said.

8
00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.168
He glanced toward Wyssa.

9
00:00:34.188 --> 00:00:36.949
The old woman snapped her fingers and zapped out of sight.

10
00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:39.090
"Hey!" Gliss cried.

11
00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.451
"Where did she go?"

12
00:00:40.751 --> 00:00:41.331
Zann asked.

13
00:00:41.351 --> 00:00:44.072
"Maybe she'll come back," Perda said.

14
00:00:45.013 --> 00:00:47.594
They waited for a few minutes to see if Wyssa would return.

15
00:00:48.394 --> 00:00:53.716
After several minutes passed by, they decided to give up, and walked the short distance into town.

16
00:00:54.957 --> 00:00:57.758
When they got there, they saw election ads everywhere.

17
00:00:58.478 --> 00:01:01.740
Magical posters floated above almost every street corner.

18
00:01:02.576 --> 00:01:04.637
Words and images flashed on and off.

19
00:01:05.397 --> 00:01:09.279
Automatons marched around, squawking out names and slogans.

20
00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:11.380
"Vote Venna!"

21
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.741
"Laddno for king!"

22
00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:19.283
Zann glanced up and saw Laddno's name written in the sky in glowing letters.

23
00:01:19.303 --> 00:01:22.465
"This is crazy," he commented.

24
00:01:22.485 --> 00:01:24.285
"It sure is."

25
00:01:25.266 --> 00:01:27.567
Gliss gasped and pointed at another ad.

26
00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.368
"Look—the election is tomorrow!"

27
00:01:31.276 --> 00:01:32.777
"Tomorrow?" Zann said.

28
00:01:32.797 --> 00:01:38.079
"We must have lost even more time traveling back and forth to the Far Frontier than we realized."

29
00:01:38.779 --> 00:01:42.441
"We'd better get to Teplo's house and see what's going on," Perda said.

30
00:01:42.461 --> 00:01:45.022
"I hope Fala is still free.

31
00:01:45.582 --> 00:01:48.023
She could help us get word to Venna about Morb."

32
00:01:48.963 --> 00:01:49.703
Zann nodded.

33
00:01:49.723 --> 00:01:51.044
"I hope so.

34
00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.425
Maybe it's good that the election is tomorrow.

35
00:01:53.825 --> 00:01:57.307
As soon as it's over, Venna can focus on stopping Morb's evil plans."

36
00:01:58.227 --> 00:02:00.648
"Whatever those plans are," Darb added.

37
00:02:01.492 --> 00:02:04.233
"We still don't know what his new contraption is supposed to do."

38
00:02:04.973 --> 00:02:05.834
Gliss shivered.

39
00:02:05.854 --> 00:02:08.195
"I'm sure it's something bad.

40
00:02:08.955 --> 00:02:10.016
Come on, let's zap."

41
00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:12.497
They zapped to Teplo's neighborhood.

42
00:02:13.677 --> 00:02:15.678
Shouts rang out from a park nearby.

43
00:02:15.698 --> 00:02:21.020
"There's another Void Rights rally going on," Gliss said.

44
00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.901
"Is Laddno there?"

45
00:02:23.101 --> 00:02:23.721
Perda asked.

46
00:02:23.741 --> 00:02:26.842
"Maybe we should try to warn him about Morb.

47
00:02:27.503 --> 00:02:30.844
He should be able to get word to Venna and the others at the palace."

48
00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:32.741
They stepped closer.

49
00:02:33.821 --> 00:02:36.403
Gliss levitated to get a better look over the crowd.

50
00:02:36.423 --> 00:02:39.645
"I don't see Laddno," she reported.

51
00:02:39.665 --> 00:02:43.287
"Hey, I think that's Jev's father speaking now!"

52
00:02:43.307 --> 00:02:45.328
"Is Jev there too?"

53
00:02:45.788 --> 00:02:46.389
Darb asked.

54
00:02:46.409 --> 00:02:50.171
"Uh-huh." Gliss quickly lowered herself to the ground.

55
00:02:50.191 --> 00:02:53.033
"We should leave before Jev sees us."

56
00:02:53.893 --> 00:02:58.236
"Wait." Zann had just spotted his friend Mari standing near the back of the crowd.

57
00:02:59.104 --> 00:03:01.746
He sent his voice toward her with a Sound-shifting spell.

58
00:03:01.766 --> 00:03:03.247
"It's Zann.

59
00:03:03.547 --> 00:03:05.408
Meet me behind the crooked tree on the corner."

60
00:03:05.428 --> 00:03:10.252
"Why do you want her to come meet us?"

61
00:03:10.992 --> 00:03:13.934
Perda asked as Zann led the way to the spot he'd mentioned.

62
00:03:13.954 --> 00:03:18.937
"She can probably tell us about anything important that happened while we were away," Zann said.

63
00:03:18.957 --> 00:03:21.759
"What if the prisoners got released or something?

64
00:03:22.199 --> 00:03:24.401
Now that we're back, we should find out what to expect."

65
00:03:27.043 --> 00:03:28.804
Moments later Mari arrived.

66
00:03:29.536 --> 00:03:30.897
She looked happy to see everyone.

67
00:03:30.917 --> 00:03:34.338
"I was wondering what happened to you guys," she said.

68
00:03:34.358 --> 00:03:36.219
"I haven't seen you in days."

69
00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.701
"We, uh, were out of town," Zann said.

70
00:03:39.721 --> 00:03:41.322
"Out of town?"

71
00:03:41.722 --> 00:03:42.942
Mari sounded surprised.

72
00:03:42.962 --> 00:03:46.284
"Yeah." Perda shot a warning look at the others.

73
00:03:46.304 --> 00:03:50.146
"Um, we just wanted to stay out of sight for a while.

74
00:03:50.766 --> 00:03:54.648
We were afraid Zann might get locked up because his parents are under suspicion."

75
00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:59.892
Zann was a little surprised that Perda didn't want to tell Mari why they'd really left town.

76
00:04:00.612 --> 00:04:03.054
Maybe she thought it would take too long to explain.

77
00:04:03.875 --> 00:04:07.158
After all, they might not have much time to stop Morb.

78
00:04:07.938 --> 00:04:10.140
His contraption had appeared to be almost finished.

79
00:04:10.821 --> 00:04:14.944
And it probably wouldn't take Morb long to repair any damage the nomads had done to it.

80
00:04:14.964 --> 00:04:21.149
"Oh, right, that makes sense," Mari said, shooting Zann a sympathetic smile.

81
00:04:21.169 --> 00:04:24.912
"I don't blame you for hiding out in Swamp Bottom for a while.

82
00:04:25.512 --> 00:04:26.793
Anyway, you've missed a lot.

83
00:04:27.353 --> 00:04:29.615
People are really going crazy over this election."

84
00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:33.778
"We saw all the ads and automatons," Gliss said.

85
00:04:33.798 --> 00:04:35.919
"I've never seen so many!"

86
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:37.760
Mari nodded.

87
00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:41.043
"Like I said, people are going crazy these days.

88
00:04:41.663 --> 00:04:46.606
I just hope I can continue keeping the remaining relics safe until the election is over tomorrow," she

89
00:04:46.646 --> 00:04:51.209
said. "Venna helped me put a Security spell on your parents' lab, just in case."

90
00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:54.632
"Good," Perda said with a laugh.

91
00:04:55.472 --> 00:04:58.534
"Now you can say the future queen helped you create a spell."

92
00:04:58.554 --> 00:05:01.156
"Maybe." Mari shrugged.

93
00:05:01.176 --> 00:05:04.838
"Actually, most people think Laddno is going to win."

94
00:05:04.858 --> 00:05:07.360
"Laddno?" Zann said.

95
00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:09.982
"I can't believe—" "Hey!"

96
00:05:10.602 --> 00:05:11.663
a new voice interrupted.

97
00:05:12.864 --> 00:05:16.626
It was the young man from Wormwood—the one who'd loaned Darb the boat.

98
00:05:17.347 --> 00:05:19.168
He hurried toward them, looking annoyed.

99
00:05:19.188 --> 00:05:20.869
"Where's my boat?"

100
00:05:21.249 --> 00:05:22.270
the young man demanded.

101
00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.712
"You were supposed to bring it back!"

102
00:05:25.552 --> 00:05:26.833
"Uh-oh," Zann muttered.

103
00:05:27.514 --> 00:05:32.738
They definitely didn't have time to try to explain that they'd left the boat behind in another world.

104
00:05:32.758 --> 00:05:34.679
"Let's get out of here.

105
00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:37.401
Zap!" Splash!

106
00:05:37.421 --> 00:05:39.683
"Ugh!" Perda cried.

107
00:05:39.703 --> 00:05:43.706
"Zann, why do you always zap us into water?"

108
00:05:43.726 --> 00:05:45.367
"Never mind."

109
00:05:45.948 --> 00:05:48.850
Gliss stepped out of the shallows of the river where they'd landed.

110
00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.552
She snapped her fingers to dry her clothes.

111
00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:54.085
"Look, we're near the palace.

112
00:05:54.546 --> 00:05:57.308
Let's see if we can sneak in and see our families."

113
00:05:57.328 --> 00:05:59.389
"Good idea," Zann said.

114
00:05:59.409 --> 00:06:02.071
"I want to make sure my parents and Boz are okay."

115
00:06:03.032 --> 00:06:06.414
Zann and Gliss conjured large hats to hide their red hair.

116
00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:12.138
Then all four kids crept around the corner until they could see into the palace square.

117
00:06:12.158 --> 00:06:15.540
"Zann, are you sure this is a good idea?"

118
00:06:16.021 --> 00:06:16.641
Darb whispered.

119
00:06:16.661 --> 00:06:20.704
"Everyone is distracted by the election right now," Zann whispered back.

120
00:06:21.388 --> 00:06:26.852
"This might be our best chance to His voice trailed off, and he gasped.

121
00:06:27.733 --> 00:06:30.635
Several trolls had just stepped out of the palace!
